@startuml flow-question-to-answer
' The central flow: a question arrives, joins a topic, gets an answer, reaches the room.
'
' Render:  plantuml docs/diagrams/flow-question-to-answer.puml

title Flow — from a question asked to an answer published

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #4A5568
  LifeLineBorderColor #7C86A0
  ParticipantBorderColor #7C86A0
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FDFDFD
}

actor Attendee
participant "Angular SPA" as SPA
participant "Spring Boot" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "AI service\n(FastAPI)" as AI
actor Moderator

== Asking ==

Attendee -> SPA : types a question
SPA -> API : POST /api/questions/submit-question
activate API

API -> API : MeetingScope.activeMeetingId()
note right
  Stamped whether or not the MEETINGS
  feature is on. A question filed
  without a meeting id can never be
  put back into the right partition
  later.
end note

API -> AI : POST /ingest\n{text, attendeeId, weight, meeting_id}
activate AI
AI -> AI : embed (all-MiniLM-L6-v2, 384 dims)
AI -> AI : nearest centroid **within this meeting**
note right of AI
  Partitioned by meeting. Without it a
  question at this year's AGM folds into
  a topic from last year's — not untidy,
  simply a wrong answer, and invisible
  until somebody reads the board.
end note
AI --> API : {cluster_id, isNew}
deactivate AI

API -> DB : INSERT question (cluster_id, meeting_id)
API --> SPA : their own cluster assignment
deactivate API
SPA --> Attendee : "asked" / "merged with N others"

note over SPA, Attendee
  Returns immediately with **this** attendee's
  result. The board catches up on its own.
end note

== Ranking ==

API -> AI : GET /clusters?meeting_id=…
AI --> API : topics ranked by weight and count
API -> SPA : board push (WebSocket)\nfallback poll every 45s — SILENT, no global loader

== Answering ==

Moderator -> SPA : picks a topic, asks for a draft
SPA -> API : POST /api/clusters/draft-answer
activate API
API -> AI : POST /draft\n{cluster_id, question, meeting_id}
activate AI
AI -> AI : retrieve from FAISS,\n**filtered to this meeting + shared docs**
AI -> AI : generate, grounded, with citations
AI --> API : {answer, citations}
deactivate AI
API -> DB : UPSERT cluster_draft (published = false)
API --> SPA : draft + citations
deactivate API

Moderator -> SPA : edits, then publishes
SPA -> API : POST /api/room/publish-answer
API -> DB : cluster_draft.published = true
API -> SPA : push to every attendee board

SPA --> Attendee : the answer appears,\nwith the documents it came from

== If the AI service is down ==

SPA -> API : POST /api/chat/semantic-search
API -> AI : POST /search
AI --> API : ✗ connection refused
API --> SPA : **503** "The AI service is not available\nright now… try again shortly."
note over API
  Not a bare 500. Every AiClient call used
  to end in .block() with no handler and no
  logger, so an outage reached the SPA as
  Spring's default error page — no message
  to show, and no log line to diagnose it
  from. See AiClient.await().
end note

@enduml
